---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageLayout from "../layouts/PageLayout.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "../data/site";

const crumbs = [
  { name: "Home", url: "/" },
  { name: "Privacy Policy", url: "/privacy-policy" },
];

const lastUpdated = "2026-08-22";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How {siteConfig.name} handles data, cookies, analytics, and your privacy."
>
  <PageLayout title="Privacy Policy" breadcrumbs={crumbs} updatedDate={lastUpdated}>
    <p>Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <p>
      This privacy policy explains what information is collected when you visit
      {siteConfig.name} (“we”, “us”), how it is used, and the choices you have. This is a static
      website, so we collect remarkably little data by design.
    </p>

    <h2>Information we collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Cookies and analytics:</strong> if analytics is enabled, we may use tools such as
        Google Analytics to understand aggregate traffic (pages visited, approximate location,
        device type). This is anonymous and aggregated.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Contact messages:</strong> if you email us via our contact page, your email app
        sends us whatever you include. We use it only to reply.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Newsletter:</strong> if a newsletter is active, we collect the email address you
        submit through the sign-up form, used only for sending the newsletter.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Logs:</strong> our hosting provider (for example Hostinger) records standard server
        logs (IP address, browser, requested page) as part of normal operation.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How we use information</h2>
    <p>We use collected information to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Understand which content is most useful and improve the site;</li>
      <li>Reply to messages and send requested newsletters;</li>
      <li>Keep the site secure and operational.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Advertising and third-party services</h2>
    <p>
      We may display advertising or use third-party services (analytics, ad networks, email
      providers). These providers may use cookies or similar technologies. Advertising partners
      such as Google may use cookies to serve ads based on your prior visits. You can opt out of
      personalized advertising via{" "}
      <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" rel="noopener nofollow" target="_blank">
        Google Ads Settings
      </a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      Cookies are small files stored on your device. The site itself sets no essential cookies.
      Third-party services (analytics, ads) may set their own cookies. You can disable cookies in
      your browser at any time; the site will continue to work.
    </p>

    <h2>Data sharing</h2>
    <p>
      We do not sell your personal information. We only share data with service providers that
      help operate the site (hosting, analytics, email) and only to the extent needed.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Depending on where you live (e.g. GDPR in Europe, CCPA in California), you may have rights to
      access, correct, or delete your data, and to object to or restrict processing. To exercise
      these rights, contact us at <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.email}`}>{siteConfig.email}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>External links</h2>
    <p>
      Our articles may link to external websites. We are not responsible for their privacy
      practices. Please review their policies when you visit them.
    </p>

    <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
    <p>
      This site is intended for general audiences and is not directed at children under 13. We do
      not knowingly collect personal information from children.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy from time to time. The “last updated” date above shows when it was
      last changed. Continued use of the site after changes constitutes acceptance of the revised
      policy.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy: <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.email}`}>{siteConfig.email}</a>.
    </p>
  </PageLayout>
</BaseLayout>
